name: sim.packInt32Table
description: Packs an array of int32 numbers into a string
luaSynopsis: bytes data = sim.packInt32Table(list int32Numbers, int startInt32Index = 0, int int32Count = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer data = sim.packInt32Table(int[] int32Numbers, int startInt32Index = 0, int int32Count = 0)
inputs:
1. int32Numbers: array containing int32 numbers. Non-numbers will be packed as zero values
2. startInt32Index: zero-based index from which on data should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. int32Count: amount of int32s that should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum available int32s should be packed from the indicated startInt32Index)
outputs:
1. data: a buffer (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed int32 numbers
replacedBy:
- name: packArray, class: app, file: app_packArray.method
